    {
      "text": "⊥",
      "bbox": [
        124.1600112915039,
        322.5626525878906,
        130.3876190185547,
        329.1459045410156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "is the component of the freestream velocity perpendicular to the actuator disk, Adisk",
      "bbox": [
        138.9870147705078,
        318.0579528808594,
        518.5744018554688,
        327.8188781738281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "is the area of the actuator disk, and κ is a correction factor to deal with unmodeled losses. For",
      "bbox": [
        88.68701171875,
        330.012939453125,
        519.1923217773438,
        338.8597106933594
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "our analysis κ = 1.2. We note that this formulation does not follow Glauert’s modiﬁed momentum",
      "bbox": [
        88.68701171875,
        341.9679260253906,
        519.1969604492188,
        350.814697265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "theory for forward ﬂight (Glauert, 1927) as is done in other quadcopter modeling approaches (e.g.,",
      "bbox": [
        88.68700408935547,
        353.97271728515625,
        519.2705688476562,
        362.7696838378906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(Huang et al., 2009; Bangura and Mahony, 2017)), but rather assumes that only the free-stream",
      "bbox": [
        88.68700408935547,
        365.9277038574219,
        519.230712890625,
        374.72467041015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "velocity perpendicular to the actuator disks contributes to the generated thrust.",
      "bbox": [
        88.68700408935547,
        377.8836975097656,
        438.80267333984375,
        386.6806640625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A plot of the velocity-turning radius relationship across a set of ﬁxed-wing and quadcopter UAVs",
      "bbox": [
        100.64300537109375,
        389.83868408203125,
        519.2715454101562,
        398.6356506347656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "of diﬀerent scales can be seen in Figure 1. The lines with a color gradient represent post-stall",
      "bbox": [
        88.68700408935547,
        401.7936706542969,
        519.2904052734375,
        410.59063720703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "minimum power turns (α > 15◦). The dashed black lines represent ﬁxed-wing UAVs restricted to",
      "bbox": [
        88.68700408935547,
        411.7675476074219,
        519.22998046875,
        422.5456237792969
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the low angle-of-attack domain (α < 10◦). The solid red region are quadcopter minimum power",
      "bbox": [
        88.68699645996094,
        423.7225341796875,
        519.1721801757812,
        434.5006103515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "turns. At high angles of attack, the ﬁxed wing is capable of low turn radii maneuvers on par with",
      "bbox": [
        88.68699645996094,
        437.65863037109375,
        519.260498046875,
        446.4555969238281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the quadcopter UAV. A post-stall ﬁxed-wing UAV is also able to achieve smaller turn radii than",
      "bbox": [
        88.68699645996094,
        449.6146240234375,
        519.2406616210938,
        458.4115905761719
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "a ﬁxed-wing UAV restricted to the low angle-of-attack regime, which must dramatically increase",
      "bbox": [
        88.68699645996094,
        461.5696105957031,
        519.2305908203125,
        470.3665771484375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "speed and bank angle to minimize a turn.",
      "bbox": [
        88.68699645996094,
        473.52459716796875,
        270.94281005859375,
        482.3215637207031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "B. Energy Analysis",
      "bbox": [
        88.68699645996094,
        499.13958740234375,
        191.8245086669922,
        509.672119140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We would like determine when it is more advantageous to deploy an aerobatic ﬁxed-wing UAV",
      "bbox": [
        88.68699645996094,
        518.4215698242188,
        519.230712890625,
        527.2185668945312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "instead of other aerial systems. Even though ﬁxed wings are signiﬁcantly more energy eﬃcient in",
      "bbox": [
        88.68699645996094,
        530.3765869140625,
        519.280517578125,
        539.173583984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "steady-level ﬂight than a quadcopter, they are in general, less eﬃcient in hover. Understanding this",
      "bbox": [
        88.68699645996094,
        542.33154296875,
        519.3102416992188,
        551.1285400390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "trade-oﬀas a function of environment is particularly important in the context of heterogeneous",
      "bbox": [
        88.68699645996094,
        554.28759765625,
        519.2705078125,
        563.0845947265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "swarms since operators often desire to optimally allocate navigation tasks.",
      "bbox": [
        88.68699645996094,
        566.2425537109375,
        413.1189270019531,
        575.03955078125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "To characterize for what missions an aerobatic ﬁxed-wing UAV operating at high angles of attack",
      "bbox": [
        100.64299774169922,
        578.1975708007812,
        519.2415161132812,
        586.9945678710938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "has an energetic advantage over a quadrotor, we apply an approximate ﬁrst principles analysis of the",
      "bbox": [
        88.68699645996094,
        590.152587890625,
        519.2803955078125,
        598.9495849609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "energy consumed by a UAV navigating along a ﬂight path decomposed into straight lines and turns.",
      "bbox": [
        88.68699645996094,
        602.1075439453125,
        519.2607421875,
        610.904541015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We approximate the energy expended along a portion of the ﬂight path as",
      "bbox": [
        100.64299774169922,
        614.0625610351562,
        425.2642822265625,
        622.8595581054688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etotal = Estraight + Eturn,",
      "bbox": [
        88.68699645996094,
        632.5977783203125,
        198.80560302734375,
        642.9395751953125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(34)",
      "bbox": [
        501.36199951171875,
        632.6475830078125,
        519.0755004882812,
        641.444580078125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "where Eturn = Pturnrψturn, where ψturn is the angle of the turn, and",
      "bbox": [
        88.68701171875,
        651.1827392578125,
        385.33721923828125,
        661.5245361328125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Estraight = Estart + Estop + Ecruise",
      "bbox": [
        88.68699645996094,
        669.7677612304688,
        235.23184204101562,
        680.1095581054688
      ],
      "direction": [
